      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Section 56AB",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "Omit:\n(c)\nmay require these kinds of disclosures, and other things,\nto be done in accordance with data standards.\nsubstitute:\n(c)\nenable consumers in those sectors to request accredited\npersons to give instructions on behalf of the consumers\nto service providers in those sectors for the performance\nof actions; and\n(d)\nrequire these kinds of disclosures and other things to be\ndone, and these kinds of instructions to be given, in\naccordance with data standards.\nThis Part regulates the instruction layer associated with instructions\nfor the performance of actions, which includes regulating requests\nfor instructions, the giving of instructions, and how service\nproviders process instructions.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nIntroductory provisions  Part 1\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\nA service provider given an instruction under the rules to perform\nan action must do so if the provider ordinarily performs actions of\nthat type in the course of its business. Otherwise, this Part contains\nlittle regulation of the action layer (that is, regulating how service\nproviders perform actions they are instructed to do). For example,\nthe provider can perform the action, and charge any fees, in the\nway it ordinarily does.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "Omit:\n(c)\nmay require these kinds of disclosures, and other things,\nto be done in accordance with data standards.\nsubstitute:\n(c)\nenable consumers in those sectors to request accredited\npersons to give instructions on behalf of the consumers\nto service providers in those sectors for the performance\nof actions; and\n(d)\nrequire these kinds of disclosures and other things to be\ndone, and these kinds of instructions to be given, in\naccordance with data standards.\nThis Part regulates the instruction layer associated with instructions\nfor the performance of actions, which includes regulating requests\nfor instructions, the giving of instructions, and how service\nproviders process instructions.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nIntroductory provisions  Part 1\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\nA service provider given an instruction under the rules to perform\nan action must do so if the provider ordinarily performs actions of\nthat type in the course of its business. Otherwise, this Part contains\nlittle regulation of the action layer (that is, regulating how service\nproviders perform actions they are instructed to do). For example,\nthe provider can perform the action, and charge any fees, in the\nway it ordinarily does.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6704757b6826587b4a04a0d022c3dac7a556641e95084865892566d6a8821a9b",
      "skos:note": "Service providers must perform actions in accordance with data standards if they ordinarily do so."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Section 56AB",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Omit:\n(c)\nmay require these kinds of disclosures, and other things,\nto be done in accordance with data standards.\nsubstitute:\n(c)\nenable consumers in those sectors to request accredited\npersons to give instructions on behalf of the consumers\nto service providers in those sectors for the performance\nof actions; and\n(d)\nrequire these kinds of disclosures and other things to be\ndone, and these kinds of instructions to be given, in\naccordance with data standards.\nThis Part regulates the instruction layer associated with instructions\nfor the performance of actions, which includes regulating requests\nfor instructions, the giving of instructions, and how service\nproviders process instructions.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nIntroductory provisions  Part 1\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\nA service provider given an instruction under the rules to perform\nan action must do so if the provider ordinarily performs actions of\nthat type in the course of its business. Otherwise, this Part contains\nlittle regulation of the action layer (that is, regulating how service\nproviders perform actions they are instructed to do). For example,\nthe provider can perform the action, and charge any fees, in the\nway it ordinarily does.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
