    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-54",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "54 Subsection 56BD(1) (note 1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-54"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the note, substitute:\nNote 1:\nThis means CDR data cannot be required to be disclosed if it is only\nCDR data because it is directly or indirectly derived from:\n(a)\nother CDR data within a class specified, as described in\nparagraph 56AC(2)(a), in an instrument designating a sector\nunder subsection 56AC(2); or\n(b)\nother CDR data, about a CDR consumer for a CDR action, that\nan accredited action initiator is authorised to use to prepare or\ngive a valid instruction for the performance of the CDR action.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the note, substitute:\nNote 1:\nThis means CDR data cannot be required to be disclosed if it is only\nCDR data because it is directly or indirectly derived from:\n(a)\nother CDR data within a class specified, as described in\nparagraph 56AC(2)(a), in an instrument designating a sector\nunder subsection 56AC(2); or\n(b)\nother CDR data, about a CDR consumer for a CDR action, that\nan accredited action initiator is authorised to use to prepare or\ngive a valid instruction for the performance of the CDR action.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-54-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "93cb2a88733906b109094bd204036453aea005cc0aca4a7fc564e47b88a19b32",
      "skos:note": "Repeal note and substitute with new definition for CDR data disclosure"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-54",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "54 Subsection 56BD(1) (note 1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the note, substitute:\nNote 1:\nThis means CDR data cannot be required to be disclosed if it is only\nCDR data because it is directly or indirectly derived from:\n(a)\nother CDR data within a class specified, as described in\nparagraph 56AC(2)(a), in an instrument designating a sector\nunder subsection 56AC(2); or\n(b)\nother CDR data, about a CDR consumer for a CDR action, that\nan accredited action initiator is authorised to use to prepare or\ngive a valid instruction for the performance of the CDR action."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-54-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-54"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55 Subsection 56BD(3)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-55"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nRules affecting data holders that relate to the use, accuracy,\nstorage, security or deletion of CDR data\n(3) For a data holder of CDR data for which there are one or more\nCDR consumers, the consumer data rules:\n(a) can only include rules affecting the data holder that relate to\nthe deletion of the CDR data if:\n(i) the CDR data; or\n(ii) any other CDR data from which it was directly or\nindirectly derived;\nwas disclosed to the data holder under the consumer data\nrules; and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the power to make consumer data rules  Part 4\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\n(b) can only include rules affecting the data holder that relate to\nthe use, accuracy, storage or security of the CDR data if such\nrules also relate to the disclosure of the CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nRules affecting data holders that relate to the use, accuracy,\nstorage, security or deletion of CDR data\n(3) For a data holder of CDR data for which there are one or more\nCDR consumers, the consumer data rules:\n(a) can only include rules affecting the data holder that relate to\nthe deletion of the CDR data if:\n(i) the CDR data; or\n(ii) any other CDR data from which it was directly or\nindirectly derived;\nwas disclosed to the data holder under the consumer data\nrules; and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the power to make consumer data rules  Part 4\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\n(b) can only include rules affecting the data holder that relate to\nthe use, accuracy, storage or security of the CDR data if such\nrules also relate to the disclosure of the CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "225b5e624fbc94971b5b92d8284c12448ee57101ef0c26c8207d392f69c8a33f",
      "skos:note": "Cannot include rules affecting data holder that relate to deletion of CDR data unless disclosure under consumer data rules."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-55",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55 Subsection 56BD(3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nRules affecting data holders that relate to the use, accuracy,\nstorage, security or deletion of CDR data\n(3) For a data holder of CDR data for which there are one or more\nCDR consumers, the consumer data rules:\n(a) can only include rules affecting the data holder that relate to\nthe deletion of the CDR data if:\n(i) the CDR data; or\n(ii) any other CDR data from which it was directly or\nindirectly derived;\nwas disclosed to the data holder under the consumer data\nrules; and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the power to make consumer data rules  Part 4\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\n(b) can only include rules affecting the data holder that relate to\nthe use, accuracy, storage or security of the CDR data if such\nrules also relate to the disclosure of the CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "!",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition on rules affecting data holder that relate to deletion of CDR data unless disclosure under consumer data rules.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56 After section 56BG",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-56"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n56BGA  Rules about initiating CDR actions\nInstructions may be given to initiate types of CDR actions\n(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(ca), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n(a) requirements on an accredited action initiator for a type of\nCDR action relating to giving a valid instruction:\n(i) for the performance of a CDR action of that type; and\n(ii) to an action service provider for a CDR action of that\ntype; and\n(iii) on behalf of a CDR consumer for the CDR action, and\nin response to that consumer’s valid request; and\n(iv) after a series of specified kinds of interactions between\nthat initiator, provider, consumer or other persons\n(whether involving all or any 2 of them);\n(b) rules about how an instruction must be prepared for it to be a\nvalid instruction of the kind described in paragraph (a), what\nmatters a valid instruction may cover, and when an\ninstruction ceases to be a valid instruction;\n(c) rules about:\n(i) how a CDR consumer for a CDR action may make a\nvalid request of the kind described in\nsubparagraph (a)(iii); and\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid,\nwhat matters a valid request may cover, and when a\nrequest ceases to be a valid request;\n(d) for an accredited action initiator for a type of CDR action\nwho is acting as described in paragraph (a) to give a valid\ninstruction on behalf of a CDR consumer for a CDR action—\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n56BGA  Rules about initiating CDR actions\nInstructions may be given to initiate types of CDR actions\n(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(ca), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n(a) requirements on an accredited action initiator for a type of\nCDR action relating to giving a valid instruction:\n(i) for the performance of a CDR action of that type; and\n(ii) to an action service provider for a CDR action of that\ntype; and\n(iii) on behalf of a CDR consumer for the CDR action, and\nin response to that consumer’s valid request; and\n(iv) after a series of specified kinds of interactions between\nthat initiator, provider, consumer or other persons\n(whether involving all or any 2 of them);\n(b) rules about how an instruction must be prepared for it to be a\nvalid instruction of the kind described in paragraph (a), what\nmatters a valid instruction may cover, and when an\ninstruction ceases to be a valid instruction;\n(c) rules about:\n(i) how a CDR consumer for a CDR action may make a\nvalid request of the kind described in\nsubparagraph (a)(iii); and\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid,\nwhat matters a valid request may cover, and when a\nrequest ceases to be a valid request;\n(d) for an accredited action initiator for a type of CDR action\nwho is acting as described in paragraph (a) to give a valid\ninstruction on behalf of a CDR consumer for a CDR action—\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56-norm"
        },
