      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(3) Without limiting paragraph (1)(e), the grounds for varying,\nsuspending or revoking an accreditation could include failing to\ncomply with a requirement in this Part or in the consumer data\nrules.\nNote 1:\nThe requirements in this Part include the privacy safeguards.\nNote 2:\nAn example of a variation could be the imposition of a condition, or\nchanging the level of an accreditation.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(3) Without limiting paragraph (1)(e), the grounds for varying,\nsuspending or revoking an accreditation could include failing to\ncomply with a requirement in this Part or in the consumer data\nrules.\nNote 1:\nThe requirements in this Part include the privacy safeguards.\nNote 2:\nAn example of a variation could be the imposition of a condition, or\nchanging the level of an accreditation.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-62-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-62-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8a3032e9341e64c5a467c13c5d180c7dd75d3dd451e4d87c454b021acf883e3f",
      "skos:note": "Repeal subsection, substitute new grounds for varying accreditation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-62",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "62 Subsection 56BH(3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(3) Without limiting paragraph (1)(e), the grounds for varying,\nsuspending or revoking an accreditation could include failing to\ncomply with a requirement in this Part or in the consumer data\nrules.\nNote 1:\nThe requirements in this Part include the privacy safeguards.\nNote 2:\nAn example of a variation could be the imposition of a condition, or\nchanging the level of an accreditation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-62-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-62"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-62-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits failing to comply with requirements",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Repeal subsection, substitute new grounds",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No accreditation possible"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-63",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "63 Subsection 56BH(4)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-63"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the power to make consumer data rules  Part 4\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\n(4) If the consumer data rules include rules enabling decisions to be\nmade:\n(a) to vary, suspend or revoke an accreditation; or\n(b) to refuse to make a decision described in paragraph (a);\nthe rules must permit the making of applications to the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal for review of those decisions.\nNote 1:\nThe consumer data rules can also provide for internal review of these\ndecisions, and internal and AAT review of other decisions (see\nsection 56BJ).\nNote 2:\nThe decisions could be decisions of the Minister or of another person\n(see paragraph 56BJ(c)).",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the power to make consumer data rules  Part 4\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\n(4) If the consumer data rules include rules enabling decisions to be\nmade:\n(a) to vary, suspend or revoke an accreditation; or\n(b) to refuse to make a decision described in paragraph (a);\nthe rules must permit the making of applications to the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal for review of those decisions.\nNote 1:\nThe consumer data rules can also provide for internal review of these\ndecisions, and internal and AAT review of other decisions (see\nsection 56BJ).\nNote 2:\nThe decisions could be decisions of the Minister or of another person\n(see paragraph 56BJ(c)).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-63-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-63-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c38ac165d9300fd4feeb93d8a451ca06e67936f09afa271744046b7664e1468f",
      "skos:note": "Must permit applications for review of decisions made under consumer data rules"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-63",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "63 Subsection 56BH(4)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the power to make consumer data rules  Part 4\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\n(4) If the consumer data rules include rules enabling decisions to be\nmade:\n(a) to vary, suspend or revoke an accreditation; or\n(b) to refuse to make a decision described in paragraph (a);\nthe rules must permit the making of applications to the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal for review of those decisions.\nNote 1:\nThe consumer data rules can also provide for internal review of these\ndecisions, and internal and AAT review of other decisions (see\nsection 56BJ).\nNote 2:\nThe decisions could be decisions of the Minister or of another person\n(see paragraph 56BJ(c))."
    },
    {
