    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-64",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "64 After section 56BH",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-64"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n56BHA  Rules about approving persons to be voluntary action\nservice providers for types of CDR actions\n(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(da), the consumer data rules\nmay include the following rules:\n(a) rules for the approval of persons who apply to be action\nservice providers for one or more types of CDR actions;\n(b) the criteria for a person to be so approved;\n(c) rules providing that such approval may be granted subject to\nconditions, and that conditions may be imposed on such an\napproval after it has been granted;\n(d) rules providing that such approvals may be granted at\ndifferent levels corresponding to different risks, including the\nrisks associated with:\n(i) specified types of CDR actions; or\n(ii) specified classes of CDR data; or\n(iii) specified classes of applicants for such approvals;\n(e) rules specifying what a person approved at a particular level\nis authorised to do (or not authorised to do);\n(f) rules for the period, renewal, transfer, variation, suspension,\nrevocation or surrender of such approvals;\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n56BHA  Rules about approving persons to be voluntary action\nservice providers for types of CDR actions\n(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(da), the consumer data rules\nmay include the following rules:\n(a) rules for the approval of persons who apply to be action\nservice providers for one or more types of CDR actions;\n(b) the criteria for a person to be so approved;\n(c) rules providing that such approval may be granted subject to\nconditions, and that conditions may be imposed on such an\napproval after it has been granted;\n(d) rules providing that such approvals may be granted at\ndifferent levels corresponding to different risks, including the\nrisks associated with:\n(i) specified types of CDR actions; or\n(ii) specified classes of CDR data; or\n(iii) specified classes of applicants for such approvals;\n(e) rules specifying what a person approved at a particular level\nis authorised to do (or not authorised to do);\n(f) rules for the period, renewal, transfer, variation, suspension,\nrevocation or surrender of such approvals;\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-64-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-64-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dc5270d9a79d664a5546a6c91ddda405fc9a08954736e1d69015abc61d574b8e",
      "skos:note": "Rules for approving persons to be voluntary action service providers for types of CDR actions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-64",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "64 After section 56BH",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n56BHA  Rules about approving persons to be voluntary action\nservice providers for types of CDR actions\n(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(da), the consumer data rules\nmay include the following rules:\n(a) rules for the approval of persons who apply to be action\nservice providers for one or more types of CDR actions;\n(b) the criteria for a person to be so approved;\n(c) rules providing that such approval may be granted subject to\nconditions, and that conditions may be imposed on such an\napproval after it has been granted;\n(d) rules providing that such approvals may be granted at\ndifferent levels corresponding to different risks, including the\nrisks associated with:\n(i) specified types of CDR actions; or\n(ii) specified classes of CDR data; or\n(iii) specified classes of applicants for such approvals;\n(e) rules specifying what a person approved at a particular level\nis authorised to do (or not authorised to do);\n(f) rules for the period, renewal, transfer, variation, suspension,\nrevocation or surrender of such approvals;\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
