    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-75",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "75 After paragraph 56BP(a)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-75"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n(aa) consider the following kinds of matters in relation to making\na rule described in subsection 56BGA(2) (about fees at the\ninstruction layer) for a type of CDR action:\n(i) whether performers of actions of that type currently\ncharge fees for processing instructions to perform such\nactions;\n(ii) whether the incentive to perform actions of that type\nwould be reduced if fees could not be charged for\nprocessing such instructions;\n(iii) the marginal cost of processing such instructions in\naccordance with the consumer data rules; and",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n(aa) consider the following kinds of matters in relation to making\na rule described in subsection 56BGA(2) (about fees at the\ninstruction layer) for a type of CDR action:\n(i) whether performers of actions of that type currently\ncharge fees for processing instructions to perform such\nactions;\n(ii) whether the incentive to perform actions of that type\nwould be reduced if fees could not be charged for\nprocessing such instructions;\n(iii) the marginal cost of processing such instructions in\naccordance with the consumer data rules; and",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-75-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f24818ca386a2001446774752a50caed9f098042eb292563ca1b58a474d0cc4d",
      "skos:note": "Consider certain matters when making a rule about fees for CDR actions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-75",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "75 After paragraph 56BP(a)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n(aa) consider the following kinds of matters in relation to making\na rule described in subsection 56BGA(2) (about fees at the\ninstruction layer) for a type of CDR action:\n(i) whether performers of actions of that type currently\ncharge fees for processing instructions to perform such\nactions;\n(ii) whether the incentive to perform actions of that type\nwould be reduced if fees could not be charged for\nprocessing such instructions;\n(iii) the marginal cost of processing such instructions in\naccordance with the consumer data rules; and"
    },
    {
