    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56bv",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BV Commission may intervene if fee for disclosing or using",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-56bv"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "chargeable CDR data is unreasonable etc.\nIntervening for a class of CDR participants\n(1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, determine:\n(a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount\nof a fee, that a specified class of CDR participants for\nspecified chargeable CDR data may charge (or cause to be\ncharged) for either or both of the following matters (the\nchargeable matters):\n(i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances because of a requirement under the\nconsumer data rules to do so;\n(ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and\n(b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee;\nif the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participants\nwould otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable\nhaving regard to the criteria in subsection (4).\nIntervening for a particular CDR participant\n(2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a CDR\nparticipant for specified chargeable CDR data, determine:\n(a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount\nof a fee, that the CDR participant may charge (or cause to be\ncharged) for either or both of the following matters (the\nchargeable matters):\n(i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances because of a requirement under the\nconsumer data rules to do so;\n(ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and\n(b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee;\nif the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participant\nwould otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable\nhaving regard to the criteria in subsection (4).\nNote:\nThe determination is reviewable (see Subdivision F).\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "chargeable CDR data is unreasonable etc.\nIntervening for a class of CDR participants\n(1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, determine:\n(a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount\nof a fee, that a specified class of CDR participants for\nspecified chargeable CDR data may charge (or cause to be\ncharged) for either or both of the following matters (the\nchargeable matters):\n(i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances because of a requirement under the\nconsumer data rules to do so;\n(ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and\n(b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee;\nif the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participants\nwould otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable\nhaving regard to the criteria in subsection (4).\nIntervening for a particular CDR participant\n(2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a CDR\nparticipant for specified chargeable CDR data, determine:\n(a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount\nof a fee, that the CDR participant may charge (or cause to be\ncharged) for either or both of the following matters (the\nchargeable matters):\n(i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances because of a requirement under the\nconsumer data rules to do so;\n(ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and\n(b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee;\nif the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participant\nwould otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable\nhaving regard to the criteria in subsection (4).\nNote:\nThe determination is reviewable (see Subdivision F).\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56bv-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56bv-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "791a643df153c7bd4e28e1f0dfed8f7d5ad693fac5c43e6b1a2823ded1f2542d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-56bv",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BV Commission may intervene if fee for disclosing or using",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 31,
      "values:originalText": "chargeable CDR data is unreasonable etc.\nIntervening for a class of CDR participants\n(1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, determine:\n(a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount\nof a fee, that a specified class of CDR participants for\nspecified chargeable CDR data may charge (or cause to be\ncharged) for either or both of the following matters (the\nchargeable matters):\n(i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances because of a requirement under the\nconsumer data rules to do so;\n(ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and\n(b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee;\nif the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participants\nwould otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable\nhaving regard to the criteria in subsection (4).\nIntervening for a particular CDR participant\n(2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a CDR\nparticipant for specified chargeable CDR data, determine:\n(a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount\nof a fee, that the CDR participant may charge (or cause to be\ncharged) for either or both of the following matters (the\nchargeable matters):\n(i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances because of a requirement under the\nconsumer data rules to do so;\n(ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and\n(b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee;\nif the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participant\nwould otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable\nhaving regard to the criteria in subsection (4).\nNote:\nThe determination is reviewable (see Subdivision F).\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
