    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-93",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "93 Subsection 56ED(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-93"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the Privacy safeguards  Part 6\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\nObject\n(1) The object of this section is to ensure that each person (a CDR\nentity) who:\n(a) is a data holder of CDR data; or\n(b) is an accredited person who is or who may become an\naccredited data recipient of CDR data; or\n(c) is a designated gateway for CDR data; or\n(d) as an action service provider for a type of CDR action, has\nbeen or may be disclosed CDR data under the consumer data\nrules;\nmanages the CDR data in an open and transparent way.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the Privacy safeguards  Part 6\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\nObject\n(1) The object of this section is to ensure that each person (a CDR\nentity) who:\n(a) is a data holder of CDR data; or\n(b) is an accredited person who is or who may become an\naccredited data recipient of CDR data; or\n(c) is a designated gateway for CDR data; or\n(d) as an action service provider for a type of CDR action, has\nbeen or may be disclosed CDR data under the consumer data\nrules;\nmanages the CDR data in an open and transparent way.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-93-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-93-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-93-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "92afffec9b0fe2590640957eda765e7c235618f19e1d1bd2c02b48748a2fa169",
      "skos:note": "Ensure open and transparent management of CDR data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-93",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "93 Subsection 56ED(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 42,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the Privacy safeguards  Part 6\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\nObject\n(1) The object of this section is to ensure that each person (a CDR\nentity) who:\n(a) is a data holder of CDR data; or\n(b) is an accredited person who is or who may become an\naccredited data recipient of CDR data; or\n(c) is a designated gateway for CDR data; or\n(d) as an action service provider for a type of CDR action, has\nbeen or may be disclosed CDR data under the consumer data\nrules;\nmanages the CDR data in an open and transparent way."
    },
