    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56ef",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EF Privacy safeguard 3—soliciting CDR data from participants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-56ef"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "under the consumer data rules\n(1) A person covered by column 1 of an item of the following table\nmust not seek to collect CDR data under the consumer data rules\nfrom another person covered by column 2 of that item unless:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "under the consumer data rules\n(1) A person covered by column 1 of an item of the following table\nmust not seek to collect CDR data under the consumer data rules\nfrom another person covered by column 2 of that item unless:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56ef-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "02434264bfa33cb173f97563705cb0f95de3d312b967ddee3ddb784750204dd9",
      "skos:note": "No one can collect CDR data from another person unless specified in Schedule 1 Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-56ef",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EF Privacy safeguard 3—soliciting CDR data from participants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "under the consumer data rules\n(1) A person covered by column 1 of an item of the following table\nmust not seek to collect CDR data under the consumer data rules\nfrom another person covered by column 2 of that item unless:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56ef-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56ef"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56eg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EG Privacy safeguard 4—dealing with unsolicited CDR data from",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-56eg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "participants in CDR\n(1) A person must destroy CDR data as soon as practicable after\ncollecting it if:\n(a) the person (the collector) collected the CDR data while\ncovered by column 1 of an item of the following table, and\nfrom a person covered by column 2 of that item; and\n(b) the collector collected the CDR data:\n(i) purportedly under the consumer data rules; but\n(ii) not as the result of seeking to collect the CDR data\nunder the consumer data rules; and\n(c) the collector is not required to retain the CDR data by or\nunder an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and\n(d) in the case where item 3 of the table applies, the\ncircumstances specified in the consumer data rules do not\napply.\nDealing with unsolicited CDR data from participants in CDR\nItem\nColumn 1\nA collector who:\nColumn 2\ncollects the CDR data from:\nis an accredited person\na CDR participant for the CDR data\nas an accredited action initiator\nfor a type of CDR action\nan action service provider for that type of\nCDR action\nas an action service provider for\na type of CDR action\nan accredited action initiator for that type\nof CDR action\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly or\nindirectly from the person mentioned in column 2 of the table.\nExample:\nFor item 1 of the table, the collection could be from the CDR\nparticipant through a designated gateway (see section 56BG).",
      "skos:definition": "participants in CDR\n(1) A person must destroy CDR data as soon as practicable after\ncollecting it if:\n(a) the person (the collector) collected the CDR data while\ncovered by column 1 of an item of the following table, and\nfrom a person covered by column 2 of that item; and\n(b) the collector collected the CDR data:\n(i) purportedly under the consumer data rules; but\n(ii) not as the result of seeking to collect the CDR data\nunder the consumer data rules; and\n(c) the collector is not required to retain the CDR data by or\nunder an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and\n(d) in the case where item 3 of the table applies, the\ncircumstances specified in the consumer data rules do not\napply.\nDealing with unsolicited CDR data from participants in CDR\nItem\nColumn 1\nA collector who:\nColumn 2\ncollects the CDR data from:\nis an accredited person\na CDR participant for the CDR data\nas an accredited action initiator\nfor a type of CDR action\nan action service provider for that type of\nCDR action\nas an action service provider for\na type of CDR action\nan accredited action initiator for that type\nof CDR action\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly or\nindirectly from the person mentioned in column 2 of the table.\nExample:\nFor item 1 of the table, the collection could be from the CDR\nparticipant through a designated gateway (see section 56BG).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56eg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56eg-ss-2"
        }
