    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-102",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "102 At the end of section 56EM",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-102"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nDisclosures by action service providers\n(4) If a person as an action service provider for a type of CDR action is\nrequired or authorised under the consumer data rules to disclose\nCDR data to another person, the action service provider must:\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the Privacy safeguards  Part 6\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\nDisclosures by action service providers\n(4) If a person as an action service provider for a type of CDR action is\nrequired or authorised under the consumer data rules to disclose\nCDR data to another person, the action service provider must:\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the Privacy safeguards  Part 6\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-102-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-102-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-102-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4da6eb8cda7eaaf415c64bf498ef5617f54156e088101bde341ac45972f76d30",
      "skos:note": "Must disclose CDR data to notified consumers",
      "dc:description": "Notification of disclosure"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-102",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "102 At the end of section 56EM",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nDisclosures by action service providers\n(4) If a person as an action service provider for a type of CDR action is\nrequired or authorised under the consumer data rules to disclose\nCDR data to another person, the action service provider must:\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nChanges to the Privacy safeguards  Part 6\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024"
    },
    {
