    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-103-ss-2a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to provide accurate CDR data",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-103-ss-2a-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasValue",
      "cml:logicSummary": "CDR data has a value (accuracy, completeness)",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2A) If a person as an action service provider for a type of CDR action is required or authorised under the consumer data rules to disclose CDR data...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the action service provider must take reasonable steps to ensure that the CDR data is, having regard to the purpose for which it is held, accurate, up to date and complete."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-103-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "103(3) Subsections 56EN(3) and (4)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-103-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a person:\n(a) makes a disclosure referred to in subsection (1), (2) or (2A)\nfor a CDR consumer for CDR data; and\n(b) later becomes aware that some or all of the CDR data was\nincorrect when it was disclosed because, having regard to the\npurpose for which it was held, it was inaccurate, out of date\nor incomplete;\nthe person must advise the CDR consumer accordingly in\naccordance with the consumer data rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nBecoming aware after disclosure that the CDR data was\nincorrect—disclosing corrected CDR data",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If a person:\n(a) makes a disclosure referred to in subsection (1), (2) or (2A)\nfor a CDR consumer for CDR data; and\n(b) later becomes aware that some or all of the CDR data was\nincorrect when it was disclosed because, having regard to the\npurpose for which it was held, it was inaccurate, out of date\nor incomplete;\nthe person must advise the CDR consumer accordingly in\naccordance with the consumer data rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nBecoming aware after disclosure that the CDR data was\nincorrect—disclosing corrected CDR data",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-103"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-103-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-103-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1212b70a08eac0228e57f8879e8bc64665bb35c3caf01dfc3f8d73b126b8595b",
      "skos:note": "Must advise CDR consumer of incorrect data after becoming aware.",
      "dc:description": "Advice to CDR consumer"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-103-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "103(3) Subsections 56EN(3) and (4)",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a person:\n(a) makes a disclosure referred to in subsection (1), (2) or (2A)\nfor a CDR consumer for CDR data; and\n(b) later becomes aware that some or all of the CDR data was\nincorrect when it was disclosed because, having regard to the\npurpose for which it was held, it was inaccurate, out of date\nor incomplete;\nthe person must advise the CDR consumer accordingly in\naccordance with the consumer data rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nBecoming aware after disclosure that the CDR data was\nincorrect—disclosing corrected CDR data"
    },
