    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-105",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "105 Subsection 56EP(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-105"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nObligation on data holders and action service providers\n(1) If:\n(a) a CDR consumer for CDR data gives a request to the\nfollowing person (the CDR entity):\n(i) a data holder of the CDR data (including a request given\nthrough a designated gateway for the CDR data);\n(ii) a person as an action service provider for a type of CDR\naction; and\n(b) the request is for the CDR entity to correct the CDR data, and\nis not given in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3); and\n(c) the CDR entity was earlier required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data;\nthe CDR entity must respond to the request to correct the CDR data\nby taking such steps as are specified in the consumer data rules to\ndeal with each of the matters in subsection (3) of this section.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nSubsection 56EN(4) applies instead of this subsection if the request is\ngiven in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3).",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nObligation on data holders and action service providers\n(1) If:\n(a) a CDR consumer for CDR data gives a request to the\nfollowing person (the CDR entity):\n(i) a data holder of the CDR data (including a request given\nthrough a designated gateway for the CDR data);\n(ii) a person as an action service provider for a type of CDR\naction; and\n(b) the request is for the CDR entity to correct the CDR data, and\nis not given in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3); and\n(c) the CDR entity was earlier required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data;\nthe CDR entity must respond to the request to correct the CDR data\nby taking such steps as are specified in the consumer data rules to\ndeal with each of the matters in subsection (3) of this section.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nSubsection 56EN(4) applies instead of this subsection if the request is\ngiven in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-105-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-105-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-105-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c9dfc7e8125d2b9dd696322ad276a1740409c7608ab63de231614bd8ed1eb1eb",
      "skos:note": "Data holder must correct CDR data upon request from consumer"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-105",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "105 Subsection 56EP(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nObligation on data holders and action service providers\n(1) If:\n(a) a CDR consumer for CDR data gives a request to the\nfollowing person (the CDR entity):\n(i) a data holder of the CDR data (including a request given\nthrough a designated gateway for the CDR data);\n(ii) a person as an action service provider for a type of CDR\naction; and\n(b) the request is for the CDR entity to correct the CDR data, and\nis not given in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3); and\n(c) the CDR entity was earlier required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data;\nthe CDR entity must respond to the request to correct the CDR data\nby taking such steps as are specified in the consumer data rules to\ndeal with each of the matters in subsection (3) of this section.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nSubsection 56EN(4) applies instead of this subsection if the request is\ngiven in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3)."
    },
