    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-155",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "155 After subsection 56AO(3)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-155"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nCDR provisions apply for CDR actions to be performed inside\nAustralia\n(3A) To the extent that the CDR provisions have effect in relation to a\nCDR action to be performed within Australia, the CDR provisions\napply in relation to all persons (including foreign persons).\nExample:\nRequirements in the consumer data rules relating to giving a valid\ninstruction for the performance of a CDR action within Australia can\napply to the accredited action initiator for the CDR action even if the\naccredited action initiator is a foreign person.\nCDR provisions can apply for CDR actions to be performed\noutside Australia\n(3B) To the extent that the CDR provisions have effect in relation to an\nact, or omission, relating to a CDR action to be performed outside\nAustralia, the CDR provisions only apply if:\n(a) the act or omission is by (or on behalf of) an Australian\nperson; or\n(b) the act or omission occurs wholly or partly in Australia, or\nwholly or partly on board an Australian aircraft or an\nAustralian ship.\nExample:\nRequirements in the consumer data rules relating to giving a valid\ninstruction for the performance of a CDR action outside Australia can\napply to the accredited action initiator for the CDR action if the\naccredited action initiator is an Australian person.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nMiscellaneous amendments  Part 8\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\nCDR provisions apply for CDR actions to be performed inside\nAustralia\n(3A) To the extent that the CDR provisions have effect in relation to a\nCDR action to be performed within Australia, the CDR provisions\napply in relation to all persons (including foreign persons).\nExample:\nRequirements in the consumer data rules relating to giving a valid\ninstruction for the performance of a CDR action within Australia can\napply to the accredited action initiator for the CDR action even if the\naccredited action initiator is a foreign person.\nCDR provisions can apply for CDR actions to be performed\noutside Australia\n(3B) To the extent that the CDR provisions have effect in relation to an\nact, or omission, relating to a CDR action to be performed outside\nAustralia, the CDR provisions only apply if:\n(a) the act or omission is by (or on behalf of) an Australian\nperson; or\n(b) the act or omission occurs wholly or partly in Australia, or\nwholly or partly on board an Australian aircraft or an\nAustralian ship.\nExample:\nRequirements in the consumer data rules relating to giving a valid\ninstruction for the performance of a CDR action outside Australia can\napply to the accredited action initiator for the CDR action if the\naccredited action initiator is an Australian person.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nMiscellaneous amendments  Part 8\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-155-ss-3a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-155-ss-3b"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a2fb5d31cfe48ff3621005d0e5272b847d2aff4764826a8f3099b34d186818a9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-155",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "155 After subsection 56AO(3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nCDR provisions apply for CDR actions to be performed inside\nAustralia\n(3A) To the extent that the CDR provisions have effect in relation to a\nCDR action to be performed within Australia, the CDR provisions\napply in relation to all persons (including foreign persons).\nExample:\nRequirements in the consumer data rules relating to giving a valid\ninstruction for the performance of a CDR action within Australia can\napply to the accredited action initiator for the CDR action even if the\naccredited action initiator is a foreign person.\nCDR provisions can apply for CDR actions to be performed\noutside Australia\n(3B) To the extent that the CDR provisions have effect in relation to an\nact, or omission, relating to a CDR action to be performed outside\nAustralia, the CDR provisions only apply if:\n(a) the act or omission is by (or on behalf of) an Australian\nperson; or\n(b) the act or omission occurs wholly or partly in Australia, or\nwholly or partly on board an Australian aircraft or an\nAustralian ship.\nExample:\nRequirements in the consumer data rules relating to giving a valid\ninstruction for the performance of a CDR action outside Australia can\napply to the accredited action initiator for the CDR action if the\naccredited action initiator is an Australian person.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nMiscellaneous amendments  Part 8\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024"
    },
