    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-158",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "158 Subsections 56AR(2) and (3)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-158"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nApplication to State or Territory government entities\n(2) The CDR provisions apply only in relation to an entity that:\n(a) is part of a State or Territory; or\n(b) is a body (whether or not incorporated) established for a\npublic purpose by or under a law of a State or Territory; or\n(c) is:\n(i) holding or performing the duties of an office established\nby or under a law of a State or Territory; or\n(ii) holding an appointment made under a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n(d) is an entity prescribed by the regulations in relation to a State\nor Territory;\nif the entity is declared under subsection 56AS(1) as a participating\nentity, for the State or Territory, in one or more specified\ncapacities.\nNote 1:\nThe entity is only a participating entity for those capacities specified\nin the declaration, for example, as a data holder.\nNote 2:\nFor how the CDR provisions so apply, see subsection (4).\n(3) However, whether or not such a declaration is in force for an entity\nreferred to in subsection (2), the CDR provisions apply in relation\nto the entity to the extent that:\n(a) the CDR provisions relate to a CDR consumer for CDR data,\nand the entity is a CDR consumer for CDR data (or would be\nif the entity were a person); or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nApplication to State or Territory government entities\n(2) The CDR provisions apply only in relation to an entity that:\n(a) is part of a State or Territory; or\n(b) is a body (whether or not incorporated) established for a\npublic purpose by or under a law of a State or Territory; or\n(c) is:\n(i) holding or performing the duties of an office established\nby or under a law of a State or Territory; or\n(ii) holding an appointment made under a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n(d) is an entity prescribed by the regulations in relation to a State\nor Territory;\nif the entity is declared under subsection 56AS(1) as a participating\nentity, for the State or Territory, in one or more specified\ncapacities.\nNote 1:\nThe entity is only a participating entity for those capacities specified\nin the declaration, for example, as a data holder.\nNote 2:\nFor how the CDR provisions so apply, see subsection (4).\n(3) However, whether or not such a declaration is in force for an entity\nreferred to in subsection (2), the CDR provisions apply in relation\nto the entity to the extent that:\n(a) the CDR provisions relate to a CDR consumer for CDR data,\nand the entity is a CDR consumer for CDR data (or would be\nif the entity were a person); or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-158-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-158-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "20f35a9cda66b90f37bc242773e2a9165f9b56f57cb81abc3609dfaa7010401a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-158",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "158 Subsections 56AR(2) and (3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 57,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nApplication to State or Territory government entities\n(2) The CDR provisions apply only in relation to an entity that:\n(a) is part of a State or Territory; or\n(b) is a body (whether or not incorporated) established for a\npublic purpose by or under a law of a State or Territory; or\n(c) is:\n(i) holding or performing the duties of an office established\nby or under a law of a State or Territory; or\n(ii) holding an appointment made under a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n(d) is an entity prescribed by the regulations in relation to a State\nor Territory;\nif the entity is declared under subsection 56AS(1) as a participating\nentity, for the State or Territory, in one or more specified\ncapacities.\nNote 1:\nThe entity is only a participating entity for those capacities specified\nin the declaration, for example, as a data holder.\nNote 2:\nFor how the CDR provisions so apply, see subsection (4).\n(3) However, whether or not such a declaration is in force for an entity\nreferred to in subsection (2), the CDR provisions apply in relation\nto the entity to the extent that:\n(a) the CDR provisions relate to a CDR consumer for CDR data,\nand the entity is a CDR consumer for CDR data (or would be\nif the entity were a person); or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
