      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR provisions apply to a person if:\n(a) the person is a corporation; or\n(b) the person is not a corporation, but the person:\n(i) acts; or\n(ii) omits to act;\nin a way that affects, is capable of affecting or is taken with\nintent to affect the activities, functions, relationships or\nbusiness of a corporation.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of corporation, see subsection 4(1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The CDR provisions apply to a person if:\n(a) the person is a corporation; or\n(b) the person is not a corporation, but the person:\n(i) acts; or\n(ii) omits to act;\nin a way that affects, is capable of affecting or is taken with\nintent to affect the activities, functions, relationships or\nbusiness of a corporation.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of corporation, see subsection 4(1).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56gf"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56gf-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56gf-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ae9bfcde0910c19c5157e3fb3f23c5df23e72efc63b59a52a516f14869a88d8b",
      "skos:note": "A person is subject to the CDR provisions if they act or omit to act in a way that affects a corporation's activities."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-56gf-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56GF(1) Application of the CDR provisions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR provisions apply to a person if:\n(a) the person is a corporation; or\n(b) the person is not a corporation, but the person:\n(i) acts; or\n(ii) omits to act;\nin a way that affects, is capable of affecting or is taken with\nintent to affect the activities, functions, relationships or\nbusiness of a corporation.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of corporation, see subsection 4(1)."
    },
    {
