    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56gf-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56GF(2) Application of the CDR provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-56gf-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The CDR provisions also apply to:\n(a) a person (whether or not a corporation) acting or omitting to\nact in the course of, or in relation to, the carrying on of:\n(i) a postal, telegraphic, telephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(v) of the\nConstitution); or\n(ii) the business of banking, other than State banking\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiii) of the\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nMiscellaneous amendments  Part 8\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\nConstitution) not extending beyond the limits of the\nState concerned; or\n(iii) the business of insurance, other than State insurance\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiv) of the\nConstitution) not extending beyond the limits of the\nState concerned; or\n(b) a person (whether or not a corporation):\n(i) making a supply or communication; or\n(ii) conducting an activity or otherwise doing something;\nusing a postal, telegraphic, telephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(v) of the Constitution);\nor\n(c) a person (whether or not a corporation) acting or omitting to\nact in the course of, or in relation to:\n(i) trade or commerce between Australia and places outside\nAustralia; or\n(ii) trade or commerce among the States; or\n(iii) trade or commerce within a Territory, between a State\nor Territory or between 2 Territories; or\n(d) an individual who is being, has been or is at risk of being\nsubjected to interference, or attacks, of the kind described in\nparagraph 1 of Article 17 of the ICCPR; or\n(e) a person (whether or not a corporation) who is undertaking,\nhas undertaken or could undertake interference, or attacks, of\nthe kind described in paragraph 1 of Article 17 of the ICCPR.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The CDR provisions also apply to:\n(a) a person (whether or not a corporation) acting or omitting to\nact in the course of, or in relation to, the carrying on of:\n(i) a postal, telegraphic, telephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(v) of the\nConstitution); or\n(ii) the business of banking, other than State banking\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiii) of the\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nMiscellaneous amendments  Part 8\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\nConstitution) not extending beyond the limits of the\nState concerned; or\n(iii) the business of insurance, other than State insurance\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiv) of the\nConstitution) not extending beyond the limits of the\nState concerned; or\n(b) a person (whether or not a corporation):\n(i) making a supply or communication; or\n(ii) conducting an activity or otherwise doing something;\nusing a postal, telegraphic, telephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(v) of the Constitution);\nor\n(c) a person (whether or not a corporation) acting or omitting to\nact in the course of, or in relation to:\n(i) trade or commerce between Australia and places outside\nAustralia; or\n(ii) trade or commerce among the States; or\n(iii) trade or commerce within a Territory, between a State\nor Territory or between 2 Territories; or\n(d) an individual who is being, has been or is at risk of being\nsubjected to interference, or attacks, of the kind described in\nparagraph 1 of Article 17 of the ICCPR; or\n(e) a person (whether or not a corporation) who is undertaking,\nhas undertaken or could undertake interference, or attacks, of\nthe kind described in paragraph 1 of Article 17 of the ICCPR.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56gf"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56gf-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56gf-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3c44f6f0d65dadf964af6bbca1006d80c5a0afbf5b2b9475eff7b554c6ba7ef6",
      "skos:note": "The CDR provisions apply to certain persons acting or omitting to act in specific courses of conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024#sch-1-sec-56gf-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56GF(2) Application of the CDR provisions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The CDR provisions also apply to:\n(a) a person (whether or not a corporation) acting or omitting to\nact in the course of, or in relation to, the carrying on of:\n(i) a postal, telegraphic, telephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(v) of the\nConstitution); or\n(ii) the business of banking, other than State banking\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiii) of the\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nMiscellaneous amendments  Part 8\nNo. 75, 2024\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2024\nConstitution) not extending beyond the limits of the\nState concerned; or\n(iii) the business of insurance, other than State insurance\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiv) of the\nConstitution) not extending beyond the limits of the\nState concerned; or\n(b) a person (whether or not a corporation):\n(i) making a supply or communication; or\n(ii) conducting an activity or otherwise doing something;\nusing a postal, telegraphic, telephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(v) of the Constitution);\nor\n(c) a person (whether or not a corporation) acting or omitting to\nact in the course of, or in relation to:\n(i) trade or commerce between Australia and places outside\nAustralia; or\n(ii) trade or commerce among the States; or\n(iii) trade or commerce within a Territory, between a State\nor Territory or between 2 Territories; or\n(d) an individual who is being, has been or is at risk of being\nsubjected to interference, or attacks, of the kind described in\nparagraph 1 of Article 17 of the ICCPR; or\n(e) a person (whether or not a corporation) who is undertaking,\nhas undertaken or could undertake interference, or attacks, of\nthe kind described in paragraph 1 of Article 17 of the ICCPR."
    },
